{% elif kind == 'reference' %}
# Instructions

The sole audit target is state.checks.{{ name }}. Locate it by source_order in local_raw_evidence.target_page.layouts, or by its definition record for a definition check. Other checks are parallel questions; their errors must not invalidate this one.

Audit only the current target decision identified by checks. Neighboring pages are read-only context; their independent errors do not invalidate the target. Do not proofread typos, calculate formulas, judge author opinions, invent absent text or audit final heading levels. FAIL requires a concrete, locatable error repairable through ownership, continuation or an existing reference relationship. Vague suspicion is not an error.

Check only the literal correspondence of existing references in this source, not paragraph continuation, completeness of the original or whether the note explains the prose. raw_text is the original. Each ⟦REF⟧ in analysed_text replaces a printed reference marker. Match them in occurrence order to references. path is an internal XML path, not a character position or footnote number.

Compare each replaced original marker with definition.mark of its references target. definition.index is internal numbering and may differ from the printed mark. Markdown backslash escaping and inline-math wrappers are not part of the printed marker. Other sentences, formulas and ordinary numbers in the original are not reference-correspondence errors.

No ⟦REF⟧ and an empty references list do not imply an error; not every body source must cite a footnote. Report a missing reference only when this original source clearly contains a genuine footnote marker matching a definition mark on the same page but no corresponding reference was created. Do not force matches for author-year citations, bibliographic references, chapter-end notes or numbers that do not correspond to existing marks. Do not invent absent definitions.

Reject only with concrete literal evidence of a wrong target, displaced replacement or missing mapping. Do not reject because the target ending is unfinished, a neighboring source is wrong, a definition has no body citation, one definition is referenced repeatedly or its explanation is off topic.


literal_edits lists literal changes from original to analysed text: original is removed text, analysed is inserted text, and before/after preserve the location context. references lists targets in ⟦REF⟧ occurrence order; target_definitions supplies printed marks of same-page definitions. This list is raw evidence to audit, not a correctness verdict. Judge only whether this source preserves the reference identity and original location. Whitespace, escaping or math wrappers do not change the identity of the same printed marker.

# True

The specified existing structural decision is valid, or the evidence is insufficient to require correction.

# False

The specified decision has a clear, locatable and structurally repairable error.

